  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q69-74-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $0^\\circ\\le\\theta\\le180^\\circ$. Find the value(s) of $\\theta$ so that the following equations are true.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q69-74-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta-\\cos85^\\circ=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=5^\\circ,175^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=\\cos85^\\circ\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\sin5^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nSine is positive in quadrants I and II.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=5^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ-5^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=5^\\circ,175^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q69-74-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta\\tan20^\\circ=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=70^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\tan20^\\circ}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\cot20^\\circ\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\tan70^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is positive only in quadrant I within the given interval.\n$$\\theta=70^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q69-74-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta+\\cos80^\\circ=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No solution in $[0^\\circ,180^\\circ]$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=-\\cos80^\\circ\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\sin10^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe right-hand side is negative, but $\\sin\\theta\\ge0$ throughout $[0^\\circ,180^\\circ]$. Therefore, there is no solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q69-74-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta\\tan15^\\circ=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=105^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{\\tan15^\\circ}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=-\\cot15^\\circ\\\\\\tan\\theta&=-\\tan75^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is negative in quadrant II within the given interval.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-75^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=105^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q69-74-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta\\tan125^\\circ=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=145^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\tan125^\\circ}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\cot125^\\circ\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\tan(90^\\circ-125^\\circ)\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\tan(-35^\\circ)\\\\\\tan\\theta&=-\\tan35^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is negative in quadrant II within the given interval.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-35^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=145^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q69-74-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=\\sin200^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=110^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\cos(90^\\circ-200^\\circ)\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\cos(-110^\\circ)\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\cos110^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nCosine takes this value once in $[0^\\circ,180^\\circ]$.\n$$\\theta=110^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
